---
/**
 * Resource Packs Hub Page
 */
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro"
import Breadcrumb from "../../components/Breadcrumb.astro"

Astro.locals.cache(300)
---

<PageShell
  title="Minecraft Resource Packs | GDLauncher"
  description="Browse and install Minecraft resource packs and texture packs from CurseForge and Modrinth."
  keywords="minecraft resource packs, texture packs, curseforge resource packs, modrinth resource packs, gdlauncher"
>
    <main class="py-8">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: "Resource Packs" }]} maxWidth="max-w-6xl" />

      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="bg-darkSlate-800 rounded-xl p-8 md:p-12 mb-12">
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-lightSlate-50 mb-4">
            Minecraft
            <span class="text-primary-300">Resource Packs</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100 text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            Resource packs change how Minecraft looks with new textures, sounds, and fonts.
            No mods required - works with vanilla Minecraft.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-lightSlate-50">What are Resource Packs?</h2>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Resource packs (formerly texture packs) replace Minecraft's default visuals and audio.
            They can completely change the game's style without adding any new content.
          </p>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">Resource packs can include:</p>
          <ul class="text-darkSlate-100">
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">HD Textures</strong> - Higher resolution block and item textures</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Stylized Looks</strong> - Cartoon, realistic, or themed appearances</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Connected Textures</strong> - Seamless glass, bookshelves, and more</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Custom Sounds</strong> - New music, ambient sounds, and effects</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">3D Models</strong> - Items and blocks with custom 3D shapes</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-lightSlate-50">Resolution Tiers</h2>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Resource packs come in different resolutions, measured in pixels per block face:
          </p>
          <ul class="text-darkSlate-100">
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">16x</strong> (Vanilla default) - Runs on any hardware, classic pixel art style</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">32x</strong> - Subtle improvement, minimal performance impact</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">64x</strong> - Noticeable detail increase, needs decent hardware</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">128x</strong> - High detail, needs a good GPU</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">256x-512x</strong> - Extreme detail, needs powerful hardware and OptiFine or Continuity mod</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Higher resolutions use more VRAM. A 256x pack might use 2-4GB of VRAM compared to 500MB for vanilla textures.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-lightSlate-50">Advanced Features</h2>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Modern resource packs can include advanced features that may require additional mods:
          </p>
          <ul class="text-darkSlate-100">
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Connected Textures</strong> - Glass and bookshelves blend seamlessly (requires OptiFine or Continuity mod)</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Custom Item Textures (CIT)</strong> - Renamed items get unique textures (requires OptiFine or CIT Resewn mod)</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Animated Textures</strong> - Flowing lava, waving plants, glowing effects</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Custom Entity Models (CEM)</strong> - Reshaped mobs and items (requires OptiFine or Entity Model Features mod)</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">PBR/POM Textures</strong> - Realistic lighting and depth effects (requires shader support)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Check the resource pack description to see if it requires any mods for full functionality.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <div class="bg-darkSlate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center">
            <div class="p-8 lg:p-12">
              <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-lightSlate-50 mb-4">Browse Resource Packs in GDLauncher</h2>
              <p class="text-darkSlate-100 mb-6">
                Find and install resource packs from CurseForge and Modrinth directly in GDLauncher.
                Transform your game's look with just a few clicks.
              </p>
              <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 mb-8">
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-darkSlate-50">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-400 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                  <span>Browse thousands of texture packs</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-darkSlate-50">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-400 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                  <span>Preview packs before installing</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-darkSlate-50">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-400 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                  <span>Easy management and updates</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
              <a href="/download/windows" data-astro-prefetch="false" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-primary-500 hover:bg-primary-600 text-lightSlate-50 font-semibold transition-colors transition-transform duration-100 ease-spring active:scale-95">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M3 12V6.75l6-1.32v6.48L3 12zm17-9v8.75l-10 .15V5.21L20 3zM3 13l6 .09v6.81l-6-1.15V13zm17 .25V22l-10-1.91V13.1l10 .15z"/></svg>
                Download GDLauncher
              </a>
            </div>
            <div class="relative">
              <img
                src="https://cdn.gdl.gg/assets/website-browse-resourcepacks.jpg"
                alt="GDLauncher resource pack browser interface"
                class="w-full h-auto"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8 bg-darkSlate-800 rounded-xl p-8 md:p-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-lightSlate-50 mb-6 text-center">Learn More</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          <a href="/guides/install-resourcepacks" class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-darkSlate-700/50 hover:bg-darkSlate-700 transition-colors transition-transform duration-100 ease-spring active:scale-98">
            <span class="text-lightSlate-50 font-medium">How to Install Resource Packs</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/guides/install-shaders" class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-darkSlate-700/50 hover:bg-darkSlate-700 transition-colors transition-transform duration-100 ease-spring active:scale-98">
            <span class="text-lightSlate-50 font-medium">How to Install Shaders</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
      </div>
    </main>
</PageShell>
